{"ts": "2026-11-24T16:55:01.846761Z", "run_id": "r-20261124T1654Z-97e6", "unit": "openspec:add-web-tools", "seq": 5, "type": "task.started", "task": "3.1", "title": "3.1 Write `web/src/tools/register-pages.test.ts` (scenario \"The registration page carries fixed names and its own feature file\"; it reads the feature file and the pages as `pages.test.ts` does, `existsSync(url) ? readFileSync(url, \"utf8\") : \"\"`, so a file missing at red fails by assertion) first, and `e2e/test_m7_tool_registration.py` in the same task (a red step cannot run `e2e/`; four tests, replies and steps of test-plan-browser.md, proving the scenarios \"An MCP server is registered and a code-block server shows no credential form\", \"An OpenAPI document is previewed, given effects and registered\" \"A credential is stored and rotated and its secret never shows\" and \"A document and a code block are replaced from the server detail\"; each calls `watch_csp` and `assert_layout`; their criteria stay out of `criteria_ids`, the verifier checks them), then implement the constants, create `RegisterPage.tsx`, `CredentialSection.tsx` (design 4), `ReplaceSection.tsx` (design 7) and `web/src/features/67-admin-tool-register.tsx`, and edit `ServersPage.tsx` (the link in `PageHeader` `actions`, `CredentialSection` after the region \"Surface\", `ReplaceSection` after it; no `<ConfirmDialog` and no `data-tone=\"primary\"` is added there) and `GrantsPage.tsx` (`tools.value.refs`, `toolListNote` as a `<p>` in the \"New grant\" section); style with the kit and token utilities, no CSS file; `pages.test.ts`, `states.test.ts`, `servers.test.ts` and `tools-pages-restyle.test.ts` stay green"}
